WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.916
Zann's friends headed toward the wormhole. Zann noticed that Gliss' arms and legs were shaking.

2
00:00:06.917 --> 00:00:12.306
He winced, remembering how painful it had looked when she'd ripped off the magical goggles.

3
00:00:12.307 --> 00:00:16.528
"Wait," he said to his friends. "Are you sure you want to come with me?

4
00:00:16.529 --> 00:00:23.459
I mean, really sure? It could be dangerous. Especially if Morb is involved."

5
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.618
"Of course we're sure," Perda said. "Right, guys?"

6
00:00:27.619 --> 00:00:30.904
Gliss was still trembling, but she smiled.

7
00:00:30.905 --> 00:00:37.488
"You'd better not quit now, Zann. I don't want to think I defied Wyssa's command for nothing!"

8
00:00:37.489 --> 00:00:43.990
"Yeah." Darb took Gliss' hand. "Besides, we make a good team. And we want to help.""Okay.

9
00:00:43.991 --> 00:00:48.298
Thanks." Zann glanced at the wormhole. "But

10
00:00:48.299 --> 00:00:53.460
we don't have Wyssa to guide us anymore. We need a plan." "Good

11
00:00:53.461 --> 00:01:00.499
point." Perda paced back and forth in front of the wormhole. "Does anyone have any good ideas?" "Wyssa

12
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.380
said Morb left a bunch of terrified worlds behind him," Darb said. "Maybe

13
00:01:05.381 --> 00:01:11.514
we could start visiting worlds and asking people about Morb. That might give us some clues." Zann

14
00:01:11.515 --> 00:01:16.321
shook his head. "I'm not sure we should visit worlds randomly. We

15
00:01:16.322 --> 00:01:20.653
might end up back in that no-magic world again." Perda

16
00:01:20.654 --> 00:01:26.998
shuddered. "Or Fardark, or stinky Niffia, or that crazy cloud world." She

17
00:01:26.999 --> 00:01:32.737
was still pacing. Just then her foot hit a stone, which tumbled toward Zann. "Hey,

18
00:01:32.738 --> 00:01:37.553
check it out," said Zann, bending down to pick up the stone. "This

19
00:01:37.554 --> 00:01:41.305
looks just like my message stone!" Perda

20
00:01:41.306 --> 00:01:45.892
shrugged. "So what? It looks like a stone." "No,

21
00:01:45.893 --> 00:01:50.340
I mean I think they're the same type of stone." Zann

22
00:01:50.341 --> 00:01:54.286
fished out his message stone. It still felt warm. He

23
00:01:54.287 --> 00:01:58.410
held the two stones side by side. "See?" "Weird,"

24
00:01:58.411 --> 00:02:02.032
Darb said. "They do look alike." Gliss

25
00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:07.334
glanced around. "Look, there are more stones like that!" She

26
00:02:07.335 --> 00:02:12.426
was right. Dozens of similar stones lay near the wormhole. "I

27
00:02:12.427 --> 00:02:20.917
assumed my stone came from the Cave of the Unknown because I'd never seen one like it anywhere else in Magica," said Zann. "But

28
00:02:20.918 --> 00:02:24.580
maybe it actually came from this world." "That

29
00:02:24.581 --> 00:02:29.158
makes sense," Darb said. "This is Wyssa's home world, right? That's

30
00:02:29.159 --> 00:02:33.929
probably why she used that stone to communicate with your parents." "And

31
00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:41.648
with Morb," Perda added. "It also explains why none of us had ever heard of message stones before." "Teplo

32
00:02:41.649 --> 00:02:45.451
and Boz knew about them," Gliss pointed out. Perda

33
00:02:45.452 --> 00:02:52.383
shrugged. "They're Magic Masters. It's their job to know lots of obscure stuff." Zann

34
00:02:52.384 --> 00:02:55.056
squeezed the stone in his hand. If

35
00:02:55.057 --> 00:03:02.602
his stone came from this world, that might explain why he'd had that extra-vivid dream here earlier. "I

36
00:03:02.603 --> 00:03:09.428
think we should look for a place to play my parents' message again," he said. "There might be more clues." "Clues?

37
00:03:09.429 --> 00:03:14.296
Like what?" Perda sounded dubious. "I

38
00:03:14.297 --> 00:03:19.587
don't see any place to plug in the stone," said Gliss, looking around.

39
00:03:19.588 --> 00:03:24.260
"She’s right," Perda said. "Anyway, I just thought of another plan.

40
00:03:24.261 --> 00:03:29.068
We should try to follow Wyssa. She's looking for Morb, right?

41
00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:31.824
And Morb is looking for Zann's parents.

42
00:03:31.825 --> 00:03:36.911
So if we can catch up to Wyssa, we might find Zann's parents too."

43
00:03:36.912 --> 00:03:40.150
"Wyssa left a while ago, though," Darb said.

44
00:03:40.151 --> 00:03:43.134
"We'll never find her in the vortex now."

45
00:03:43.135 --> 00:03:47.184
"Besides, how do we know we can trust her?" Zann asked.

46
00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:50.760
"Wyssa was the one who brought those flizzes to Morb.

47
00:03:50.761 --> 00:03:54.528
She also tried to bring him a scatter beast."

48
00:03:54.529 --> 00:03:59.317
"That was earlier," Perda said. "She's not working with Morb anymore."

49
00:03:59.318 --> 00:04:03.301
Darb shrugged. "Still, she may not be on our side.

50
00:04:03.302 --> 00:04:08.535
She broke Zann's Shackle spell and put that nasty spell on Gliss, remember?"

51
00:04:08.536 --> 00:04:16.622
Gliss nodded. "Plus, she used a Truth spell on Zann without his consent, and—oh! That's it!"

52
00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:19.226
"That's what?" Perda asked.

53
00:04:19.227 --> 00:04:29.438
Gliss pointed at Zann's forehead. "Look! When Wyssa touched Zann's face to do the Truth spell, she left purple fingerprints on his skin!"

54
00:04:29.439 --> 00:04:33.790
"She did?" Zann said, reaching up to wipe away the marks.

55
00:04:33.791 --> 00:04:39.862
"Stop!" Perda leaped forward, grabbing Zann's hands before he could touch his forehead.

56
00:04:39.863 --> 00:04:48.502
"Don't wipe them off. Maybe we can use that purple stuff to track Wyssa the same way she used it to track Gliss and Darb!"

57
00:04:48.503 --> 00:04:53.008
"I was thinking the same thing," said Gliss with a smile.

58
00:04:53.009 --> 00:05:00.327
"You mean we can figure out which wormholes have been used recently, and see if she's in those worlds?" Zann said.

59
00:05:00.328 --> 00:05:06.712
Perda looked excited. "It's the only good plan we have. What do you say, Zann?"

60
00:05:06.713 --> 00:05:10.087
Zann turned his message stone over in his hand.

61
00:05:10.088 --> 00:05:14.066
"You're right," he said. "Let's not waste any more time."

62
00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:21.444
"Okay." Gliss glanced at the wormhole. "We'd better make sure we're all shackled together this time.

63
00:05:21.445 --> 00:05:24.397
We don't want to get separated again."

64
00:05:24.398 --> 00:05:29.140
"Good idea." Perda held out her hands. "Join friction, everyone.

65
00:05:29.141 --> 00:05:34.661
We'll make this one a Mutual Shackle spell so any of us can break it if we need to."

66
00:05:34.662 --> 00:05:38.558
"Just don't do that in the vortex," Zann warned.

67
00:05:38.559 --> 00:05:41.502
Soon the four of them were shackled together.

68
00:05:41.503 --> 00:05:44.683
Zann even conjured a harness for Zing.

69
00:05:44.687 --> 00:05:47.083
"Everyone ready?" Darb asked.

70
00:05:47.084 --> 00:05:51.134
"Let's go!" Perda said, leading the way toward the wormhole.

71
00:05:51.135 --> 00:05:55.749
Zann held his breath as they all dived into the vortex.

72
00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.876
It felt much scarier being there without Wyssa.

73
00:05:58.877 --> 00:06:01.333
But he tried not to think about that.

74
00:06:01.334 --> 00:06:08.547
"It's working!" Gliss cried, staring at Zann's forehead. "The fingerprints are glowing!"

75
00:06:08.548 --> 00:06:11.731
Zann's left hand was shackled to Perda.

76
00:06:11.732 --> 00:06:15.541
He used his right hand to grab the nearest wormhole.

77
00:06:15.542 --> 00:06:19.773
"Hang on, everyone!" he cried as he yanked his friends through.

78
00:06:19.774 --> 00:06:27.951
He felt the familiar sensation of passing through the wormhole. It felt weird but not unpleasant.

79
00:06:27.952 --> 00:06:29.094
Splash!

80
00:06:29.095 --> 00:06:39.821
"Drat! Aah!" Zann screamed in horror. They had just landed in a pool of boiling water!

